---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import verification from '../../../../../public/equipment/01-02/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/01-02/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/01-02/';
const fields=[['lengthMm','Length X (mm)',5,120,40],['heightMm','Height Y (mm)',5,120,20],['depthMm','Depth Z (mm)',5,120,10],['sigmaSm','Conductivity (S/m)',.01,10,2],['leftV','Left electrode (V)',-20,20,5],['rightV','Right electrode (V)',-20,20,0]];
const show=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(typeof v==='number'?Number(v.toPrecision(7)):String(v))).join('; ');
const checks=Array.isArray(verification)?verification:verification.cases;
---
<Layout pageTitle="Multiphysics workstation" subtitle="" description="Solve and inspect a passive homogeneous conducting slab on an interactive 3D workstation." wide={true}>
<article id="slab" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/01-02/">← Equipment 01-02</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#slab-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">01-02 / Multiphysics workstation / Electrical adapter</p><h2>Multiphysics workstation</h2><p>Solve the electrical potential and current through a uniform conducting slab. The ready example returns <strong>50 mA</strong> and <strong>2.5 V</strong> at the center. Swap the end-face potentials to reverse the current.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the console</h3><div id="slab-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Controls','Screens'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="slab-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="slab-model" aria-label="Orbitable metric workstation with live solving screen, yellow grid control and red voltage swap"></canvas><p id="slab-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the left monitor to solve, the yellow keypad to cycle mesh resolution, or the red switch to swap the potentials. Drag to orbit; scroll or pinch to zoom. The form mirrors these actions.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Configure the slab and solve</h3><form id="slab-form" novalidate><div class="e-fields"><label>Slab ID<input name="sampleId" value="uniform-slab-01" maxlength="96" required/></label>{fields.map(([k,t,l,h,v])=><label>{t}<input name={k} type="number" min={l} max={h} step="any" value={v}/></label>)}<label>X subdivisions<select name="nx">{[8,16,32,64].map(n=><option value={n} selected={n===16}>{n}</option>)}</select></label></div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="slab-run" class="e-run" type="submit">Solve example</button><button id="slab-grid" type="button">Cycle mesh</button><button id="slab-reverse" type="button">Swap potentials</button><button id="slab-reset" type="button">Restore example</button></div></form><p id="slab-status" role="status">Ready for the first solve.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read potential and current</h3><p id="slab-result" role="status">Run the solver to read current and potential.</p><svg id="slab-chart" viewBox="0 0 410 220" role="img" aria-label="Slab potential in volts along X in millimeters"></svg><div class="e-row"><button id="slab-json" disabled>Field JSON</button><button id="slab-csv" disabled>Field CSV</button></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><caption>Mesh refinement against the analytic reference</caption><thead><tr><th>Cells X × Y</th><th>Current error (A)</th><th>Maximum potential error (V)</th><th>Relative residual</th></tr></thead><tbody id="slab-study"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section><h3>Scope and physical model</h3><p>This is an original software workstation, not a model, license or reproduction of COMSOL, FEBio or NEURON. The console has a design-size 1.65 × 0.73 m desktop, an instrument tower and two displays. The specimen is drawn at the ready example’s 40 × 20 × 10 mm, while its visual fixture stays put when numerical dimensions change.</p>
<div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original design: dual display workstation"/><figcaption>Original geometry. Left display runs the experiment; right display shows boundaries.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original design: controls and bench slab"/><figcaption>Original geometry. Change mesh resolution at the center keypad or reverse applied end potentials at the red switch.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>Steady, homogeneous Ohmic conduction only. The solver pairs <em>E</em> = −∇φ and <em>J</em> = σ<em>E</em> with ∇·<em>J</em> = 0, fixed potentials at the X ends, zero outward flux along Y and constant depth. It uses a two-dimensional finite-volume stencil solved by conjugate gradients. The analytic check is <em>I</em> = σ<em>A</em>(φ<sub>left</sub> − φ<sub>right</sub>)/<em>L</em>. The exact linear solution is representable on all tested grids, so rounding-level agreement is expected rather than decreasing discretization error. See <a href="https://web.mit.edu/6.013_book/www/chapter7/7.html">MIT, Electromagnetic Fields and Energy, chapter 7</a>.</p>
<p>Validated inputs: dimensions 5–120 mm, conductivity 0.01–10 S/m, electrode values ±20 V, and 8, 16, 32 or 64 X subdivisions. JSON reports configuration, meter coordinates, potential (V), <em>E</em><sub>x</sub> (V/m), <em>J</em><sub>x</sub> (A/m²), total current (A), mesh study and revisions. CSV contains field samples and revisions. All outputs are simulated, not instrument measurements or a tissue solver. <a href={a+'example-result.json'}>Example result</a>.</p></section>
<section id="slab-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(r=><tr><td>{r.id}</td><td>{show(r.expected)}</td><td>{show(r.actual)}</td><td>{r.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases and tolerances</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'workstation.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Interaction targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives. Optional WebXR; physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/01-02/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#slab header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#slab h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#slab section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#slab button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#slab button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#slab-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#slab-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#slab table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#slab td,#slab th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#slab figure{margin:0}#slab img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#slab caption{text-align:left}#slab input,#slab select,#slab button{min-width:0}#slab .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}</style>
